The linker errors indicate that the DAC emulator driver is not being compiled and linked into the final application, and one of the devicetree nodes for the emulator is misconfigured.

There are two issues to fix:
1.  The Kconfig file for the DAC emulator driver (`drivers/dac/Kconfig.dac_emul`) has an incorrect dependency. It uses `!DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_DAC_EMUL_ENABLED`, which prevents the driver from being enabled when a corresponding device is present in the devicetree. The `!` needs to be removed.
2.  The devicetree overlay for the test (`tests/drivers/dac/dac_emul/boards/native_sim.overlay`) is missing the `compatible = "zephyr,dac-emul";` property for the `dac_emul0` node. This prevents the build system from associating the node with the correct driver.

Here are the fixes for these issues:

drivers/dac/Kconfig.dac_emul
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
config DAC_EMUL
	bool "DAC emulator"
	default y
	depends on !DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_DAC_EMUL_ENABLED
========
config DAC_EMUL
	bool "DAC emulator"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_DAC_EMUL_ENABLED
>>>>>>>> REPLACE

tests/drivers/dac/dac_emul/boards/native_sim.overlay
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
	dac_emul0: dac-emulator-0 {
		nchannels = <4>;
		#io-channel-cells = <1>;
		status = "okay";
	};
========
	dac_emul0: dac-emulator-0 {
		compatible = "zephyr,dac-emul";
		nchannels = <4>;
		#io-channel-cells = <1>;
		status = "okay";
	};
>>>>>>>> REPLACE
